ITEMS = ((('how do i treat a nosebleed', 'what should i do for a nosebleed at home', 'what is the first thing to do for a nosebleed', 'how do you stop a nosebleed', 'how to handle a nosebleed at home', 'what helps a nosebleed stop', 'what to do when a nosebleed starts', 'how can i treat a nosebleed quickly', 'what is the best first aid for nosebleeds', 'how should i sit during a nosebleed'), 'For a nosebleed, sit upright and lean slightly forward, then pinch the soft part of the nose and breathe through your mouth. Keep the pinch steady and do not swallow blood if you can avoid it. Ask a doctor if the bleeding will not stop or keeps returning.'), (('how long should i pinch my nose for a nosebleed', 'how long does a nosebleed usually last', 'should i keep pinching a nosebleed', 'what if i let go too soon with a nosebleed', 'how long to hold a nosebleed pinch', 'is it ok to check a nosebleed repeatedly', 'how long before a nosebleed clots', 'what if a nosebleed goes on for ages', 'should i time a nosebleed', 'when to stop pinching during a nosebleed'), 'Pinch the soft part of the nose continuously for several minutes before letting go, and resist checking too early. If bleeding starts again, pinch once more. Call emergency services if bleeding remains heavy or you feel faint or short of breath.'), (('should i tilt my head back for a nosebleed', 'which actions should i avoid during a nosebleed', 'should i stuff tissue in a nosebleed', 'is lying down bad for a nosebleed', 'should i blow my nose following a nosebleed', 'can i pack a nosebleed with cotton', 'why lean forward with a nosebleed', 'should i swallow blood from a nosebleed', 'what makes a nosebleed worse', 'how to avoid choking during a nosebleed'), 'Do not tilt your head back, lie flat or pack the nose with tissue during a nosebleed, as blood can run down the throat and cause choking or sickness. Lean forward and pinch instead. Seek urgent help if blood is entering the throat in large amounts.'), (('why do i keep getting nosebleeds', 'what causes repeated nosebleeds', 'can dry air cause nosebleeds', 'why do nosebleeds happen every winter', 'what makes nosebleeds happen often', 'should i see a doctor for recurring nosebleeds', 'can allergies lead to nosebleeds', 'how to reduce frequent nosebleeds', 'what health issues cause nosebleeds', 'when to investigate repeated nosebleeds'), 'Recurring nosebleeds can follow dry air, nose rubbing, allergies or fragile vessels, and sometimes a blood condition. Keep the nose moist and avoid picking. Ask a doctor to check if they are frequent, heavy or happen without an obvious cause.'), (('how do i treat a nosebleed in a child', 'what to do when my child has a nosebleed', 'can babies get nosebleeds', 'should i take a child to hospital for a nosebleed', 'how to calm a child with a nosebleed', 'what if a child gets nosebleeds often', "how to hold a child's nose during a nosebleed", 'is a nosebleed dangerous for a toddler', "what to do after a child's nosebleed stops", 'when to call help for a child with nosebleeds'), 'Sit the child upright, lean them forward and gently pinch the soft part of the nose while they stay calm. Reassure them and check that they are not swallowing much blood. Call a doctor if bleeding is heavy, follows an injury or happens repeatedly.'), (('what if a nosebleed follows a blow to the nose', 'should i get checked after a nosebleed from an injury', 'can a fall cause a nosebleed', 'what if the nose looks crooked after a nosebleed', 'how to treat a nosebleed after a fight', 'should i worry about a nosebleed from sport', 'what if a head injury causes a nosebleed with clear fluid', 'how to handle a nosebleed after an accident', 'can a nosebleed mean a fracture', 'when to seek help for a traumatic nosebleed'), 'A nosebleed after a blow needs the same pinching and forward lean, plus attention to any other injury. If the nose looks deformed, bleeding is heavy, or clear fluid runs from it, seek urgent assessment. Call emergency services if the person is drowsy or confused.'), (('should i take aspirin if i get nosebleeds', 'can blood thinners make nosebleeds worse', 'what if anticoagulants make a nosebleed worse', 'do tablets affect nosebleeds', 'should i stop medication because of a nosebleed', 'what to ask a pharmacist about nosebleeds', 'are nosebleeds a side effect of my medicine', 'how to handle nosebleeds with a clotting condition', 'when to call a doctor about nosebleeds and tablets', 'what if a nosebleed will not stop on warfarin'), 'Some medicines can make nosebleeds more likely or harder to stop. Do not stop prescribed tablets on your own; ask a doctor or pharmacist for advice. Call emergency services if bleeding is heavy or will not stop, and tell them about any medicines you take.'), (('how to look after myself after a nosebleed', 'should i blow my nose after a nosebleed', 'how to clean around the nose after a nosebleed', 'can i go to school after a nosebleed', 'what if a scab forms after a nosebleed', 'how to avoid another nosebleed same day', 'should i use a nasal spray after a nosebleed', 'what helps the nose heal after a nosebleed', 'can i exercise after a nosebleed', 'when to check the nose again after a nosebleed'), 'After a nosebleed, avoid blowing or rubbing the nose for a while and do not pick at any scab. A little saline spray can help if the air is dry, but ask a pharmacist first. Get medical advice if bleeding returns quickly or the nose feels blocked and painful.'), (('when should i call an ambulance for a nosebleed', 'what if pinching does not stop a nosebleed', 'how heavy does a nosebleed have to be', 'should i go to hospital for a nosebleed', 'what if i feel faint with a nosebleed', 'when to get urgent help for nosebleeds', 'what if a nosebleed follows a head injury', 'can a nosebleed block my breathing', 'what if a nosebleed makes me sick to my stomach', 'when is a nosebleed a medical emergency'), 'Call emergency services if a nosebleed is very heavy, will not stop after repeated pinching, or comes with faintness, chest pain or breathing difficulty. Seek urgent help after a head injury or if blood is running into the throat. Stay upright while waiting.'), (('how can i prevent nosebleeds', 'what helps stop nosebleeds in dry weather', 'should i use a humidifier for nosebleeds', 'can saline reduce nosebleeds', 'how to stop picking causing nosebleeds', 'what to do in winter for nosebleeds', 'does hay fever make nosebleeds worse', 'how to keep the nose moist to avoid nosebleeds', 'what habits lead to nosebleeds', 'when to ask a doctor about preventing nosebleeds'), "To reduce nosebleeds, keep the air moist, avoid picking or rubbing the nose, and treat allergies with a pharmacist's advice. Saline sprays may help when the air is dry. Ask a doctor if you get frequent bleeds despite these measures, or if they start without cause."))
